      "say": "Fresh concrete does not get strong by drying. It hardens through a chemical reaction between cement and water called hydration, and that reaction needs water for weeks. That is why builders in Delhi or Lagos spray new slabs and cover them with wet hessian. Look at the two curves on the board.",
